00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:05.030
It seems Professor Li wants to 
discuss the report you produced!

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:09.310
Once we accept that
 the medium induces time reversal,

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:11.770
the explanation isn't too complicated.

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:15.490
If we draw a diagram with 
space in the y-axis and time in the x-axis,

00:04:15.490 --> 00:04:17.030
this is what you get.

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.990
Compared to normal light that refracts like this,

00:04:19.990 --> 00:04:21.990
it would simply refract like so.

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:24.490
This presents a problem regarding energy conservation.

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:30.170
Before an incident photon reaches 
the medium, light is emitted from here.

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:33.000
At the same time, an anti-photon is created

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:37.880
that meets and annihilates the 
incident photon at the surface of the medium.

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:39.380
Sounds good so far.

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:43.600
Once the process is established, it can simply repeat.

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:47.270
By retransmitting the photon that was sent to the past,

00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:49.770
you could make the energy of 
the system continuously intensify.

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:51.150
At least on paper.

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:52.900
Sounds correct to me.

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:58.400
We call that process the Ashihara Cascade.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:00.400
I expected as much.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:02.830
You guys have already thought of all this.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.830
That was a lot of thinking for nothing.

00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:09.910
There are times when the process 
matters more than the result.

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:12.250
You envisioned all this on the spot,

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:17.260
but how many years do you think it took us 
to theorize and understand this process?

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:20.930
And that was only after deciphering Ashihara's thesis.

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:23.430
Ashihara's thesis?

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:31.850
"In the midway of this our mortal life, 
I found me in a gloomy wood, astray."

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:33.230
What's that supposed to be?

00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:35.520
Dante's descent into hell.

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:39.260
Aren't you a scientist? This is why I keep on saying:

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:39.260
Huh?

00:05:39.260 --> 00:05:41.700
You can't make fun of fairy tales, you hear me?

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:43.360
Surely you've heard of this?

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:48.450
You throw various monsters into the ocean 
and mix them together to create eternal life.

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:50.960
Amrita...

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:53.820
Or Acheron, huh?

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:56.070
I wonder who's the ferryman?

00:05:56.070 --> 00:05:56.960
What?

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:00.260
This too is Dante. The river of hell.

00:06:00.260 --> 00:06:02.300
"You shan't return once you cross."

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:07.690
The gate of hell that says 
"abandon all hope, ye who enter here."

00:06:07.690 --> 00:06:12.890
Or perhaps this is the primordial Earth's soup of life.

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:17.980
I can hardly believe we were able to uncover 
another phase of Archetype here of all places...

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:19.190
Sensor activity!

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:20.720
It's moving.

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:24.450
Just as Ashihara prophesied.

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:31.760
Fall back!

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:36.630
Sensor readings are abnormal. It's indecipherable.

00:06:36.630 --> 00:06:38.500
The search team is falling back.

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:45.680
What is that?

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:52.540
That's our culprit who rang the sensor.

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:03.110
Drop your stuff and run!

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:04.490
What? Hey!

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:10.490
If I were that Granny, I'd forget about the lot of us down 
here and prevent that thing from reaching the surface!

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:14.190
You've gotta be kidding me.

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:25.470
The monster is moving fast.

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:26.970
It'll catch up to them at this rate.

00:07:26.970 --> 00:07:29.050
Are you sure about closing the gate?

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:30.850
Make it top priority.

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:57.340
It's controlling the red dust?

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:57.340
Don't stop running!

00:07:57.340 --> 00:07:59.310
Do you wanna get imprisoned in hell?

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:20.150
That damn Granny's done it.

00:08:40.340 --> 00:08:41.130
What's wrong?

00:08:41.130 --> 00:08:42.290
Look.

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:44.000
Blood...

00:08:44.810 --> 00:08:46.960
