00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:38.260
Due to commercial and passenger flight 
restrictions, many people are currently stranded.

00:13:33.880 --> 00:13:35.670
The Rodan only continue to spread.

00:13:35.670 --> 00:13:39.340
Japan utilized their Outaki Signal. 
However, the Rodan continue to...

00:13:41.260 --> 00:13:44.600
Consider today to be a lucky day.

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:48.100
We are blessed by weather that is 
perfect for mountain hunting.

00:13:48.100 --> 00:13:52.190
To protect civilians and avert the Anguirus threat,

00:13:52.190 --> 00:13:59.740
we must pinpoint its whereabouts as soon as possible and attempt to catch or exterminate it.

00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:02.240
Fortunately for us...

00:14:02.510 --> 00:14:05.370
Speakin' of, why "Anguirus"?<i></i>

00:14:05.370 --> 00:14:06.950
It's the name of the kaiju.

00:14:07.410 --> 00:14:09.750
You know the mayor has a grandson, right?

00:14:09.750 --> 00:14:13.710
Apparently, he saw the news and called it Anguirus.

00:14:13.710 --> 00:14:17.170
Is it a slip of the tongue of "Ankylosaurus," I wonder?

00:14:17.170 --> 00:14:18.840
As for you, Mr. Outaki,

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:24.490
we want you to use the signal that lent towards 
eliminating the Rodan to corner the Anguirus into that spot.

00:14:24.490 --> 00:14:25.960
Could you do it?

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:32.890
I dunno 'bout the signal, but cornerin' the monster 
into that cage'll be a piece of cake for Jet Jaguar.

00:14:32.890 --> 00:14:35.130
Ain't it Outaki! Long time no see!

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:39.890
Yo, Gen! Ya got a big one here.

00:14:39.890 --> 00:14:41.070
A harpoon cannon?

00:14:41.070 --> 00:14:43.950
Won't your truck fly off 
if you shoot somethin' like this?

00:14:43.950 --> 00:14:45.910
Hah! Just wait and see.

00:14:45.910 --> 00:14:47.620
My instincts for victory are still sharp!

00:14:47.620 --> 00:14:49.330
That's not my point!

00:14:49.330 --> 00:14:51.580
Don't you dare forget what I'm capable of!

00:14:51.580 --> 00:14:52.750
Like I was sayin'...!

00:14:52.750 --> 00:14:55.000
O' course I'm aware of the risk!

00:15:01.310 --> 00:15:05.220
Aren't tires more stable than going bipedal?

00:15:05.220 --> 00:15:07.550
The lower half was just now thrown together.

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:09.260
We don't have time for improvements.

00:15:09.590 --> 00:15:13.890
Using generic algorithms to  
instruct it on attitude control, huh?

00:15:13.890 --> 00:15:15.770
Looks like a total mess.

00:15:16.070 --> 00:15:21.530
I'm starting from scratch after we crudely 
changed its bipedal controls to tires.

00:15:21.530 --> 00:15:24.690
So it's like a fillet that suddenly turned into wings.

00:15:27.610 --> 00:15:33.330
For a mountain hunt, this crowd sure is rowdy. 
Won't the kaiju just hide instead of showing up?

00:15:33.330 --> 00:15:39.590
Even if our nimble friend turns up, 
I doubt it'll so meekly enter its cage.

00:15:39.590 --> 00:15:43.800
Besides, even if we shoot bullets at it, 
they may reflect right back like last time.

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:45.550
Some of 'em gotta hit.

00:15:45.550 --> 00:15:48.780
Sure, it can reflect bullets, 
but it's not like its entire body is armor.

00:15:53.770 --> 00:15:54.850
That's...

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:58.690
Not only has a marine organism known as 
Manda been sighted in Japan recently,

00:15:58.690 --> 00:16:02.360
but on top of that, another kaiju 
has been spotted on ground, as well.

00:16:02.360 --> 00:16:08.040
And now, a capture operation for Anguirus, 
the new-sprung kaiju, is about to start.

00:16:07.080 --> 00:16:08.040
Hey!

00:16:08.740 --> 00:16:11.740
Wouldn't Manda net you more views?

00:16:11.740 --> 00:16:13.370
Oh, it's you guys.

00:16:13.370 --> 00:16:17.420
Weaklings like us shouldn't go to crowded places.

00:16:17.420 --> 00:16:18.350
Right?

00:16:18.960 --> 00:16:21.380
I want to see the video from back then.

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:22.790
Back then?

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:25.870
Here.

00:16:27.050 --> 00:16:29.450
What if it read the bullet's 
trajectory and reflected it back?

00:16:29.790 --> 00:16:32.010
You're saying it read the bullet's course?

00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:33.560
That's impossible.

00:16:33.560 --> 00:16:37.320
The initial velocity of a rifle bullet 
is over 900 meters per second.

00:16:37.780 --> 00:16:42.190
The distance between Anguirus and 
the gun that fired was about 20 meters.

00:16:42.190 --> 00:16:46.900
That's 0.02 seconds for the bullet 
to reach Anguirus after it was shot.

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:50.860
Nerve conduction velocity is about 
50~60 meters per second.

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:54.990
Even if it read the bullet's trajectory, 
there was no time to react before it hit.

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:57.500
Despite that, it still reflected it?

00:16:57.500 --> 00:17:02.830
What if it simply faced its back towards the 
attacker and reflected it that way?

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:04.710
It was wounded, wasn't it?

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:07.090
One of the SDF's rounds landed.

00:17:07.090 --> 00:17:09.010
Why couldn't it reflect <i>that</i> one?

00:17:09.470 --> 00:17:12.140
It didn't understand guns yet.

00:17:12.140 --> 00:17:16.570
It didn't realize a gun barrel being pointed at it
would lead to a loud noise followed by intense pain.

00:17:17.140 --> 00:17:19.150
That's why the very first shot landed.

00:17:19.150 --> 00:17:20.510
Even so...

00:17:19.940 --> 00:17:20.510
Here!

00:17:20.950 --> 00:17:24.020
Before they fired, there was motion 
in the spine it used to reflect the bullet.

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:25.900
Where? On which side?

00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:27.530
This one, maybe?

00:17:28.650 --> 00:17:32.610
It does look like it vibrated its spines before the shot...

00:17:33.450 --> 00:17:34.630
It's predicting the future.

00:17:35.370 --> 00:17:39.030
No. What if Anguirus isn't predicting the future,

00:17:39.610 --> 00:17:41.500
but seeing directly into it instead?

00:17:44.460 --> 00:17:48.390
Huh. Quite the intruiging theory you have there.

00:17:50.300 --> 00:17:51.880
Heigh-ho.

00:17:55.890 --> 00:17:58.890
Well then, this is where I take off.

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:06.330
You think he's really a journalist?

00:18:09.570 --> 00:18:11.740
Will Anguirus actually show up?

00:18:11.740 --> 00:18:15.620
Even if it does, I'm not sure if we can do anything.

00:18:15.620 --> 00:18:17.440
Residential areas are outside the perimeter.

00:18:17.440 --> 00:18:19.600
This is the only field of fire we have.

00:18:20.010 --> 00:18:23.710
Even if we get our chance,
it would need to enter our field of fire.

